IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fpine-infringements`
IMPORT `fpine-qa`

-- Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (fpine-qa.l4): every
-- exported question, for every role and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the answer
-- must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error. Each
-- question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with every value under which the situation does not
-- hold (for the stage, each document the step is not tied to), every later input ASSUMEd: the answer must be `does not
-- arise for you`. The stage helpers list every value with no OTHERWISE, so an ASSUMEd stage read through them fails.
--
-- For the person given a notice (the baseline's seat), each case is asserted twice: once against a value worked by hand
-- from the text (most taken from the baseline's cases, fpine-cases-infringements.l4: Jake's eRideable notice, k042), and
-- once against the baseline export's own answer on the same facts, with the baseline's record built here field by field
-- (`a notice with`, below, independent of the layer's own builder). For the person fined by a court the values are
-- worked by hand from the text.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked stage` IS A Stage
ASSUME `an unasked law` IS AN `Issuing law`
ASSUME `an unasked class` IS AN `ASGS remoteness class`
ASSUME `an unasked kind` IS A `Property kind`

`as the person given the notice` MEANS `I have been given an infringement notice`
`as the person fined by a court` MEANS `I have been fined by a court`

-- The baseline's record, field by field, for the comparison cases (independent of the layer's builder).
GIVEN `p0` IS A NUMBER
      `p1` IS AN `Issuing law`
      `p2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p4` IS A Stage
      `p5` IS A NUMBER
      `p6` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p7` IS A NUMBER
      `p8` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p10` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p11` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p12` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p13` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p14` IS AN `ASGS remoteness class`
      `p15` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p16` IS A BOOLEAN
      `p17` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My infringement`
`a notice with` `p0` `p1` `p2` `p3` `p4` `p5` `p6` `p7` `p8` `p9` `p10` `p11` `p12` `p13` `p14` `p15` `p16` `p17` MEANS `My infringement` WITH
    `my age at the time of the offence` IS `p0`
    `the law it was issued under` IS `p1`
    `the prosecuting authority is approved by the Registrar` IS `p2`
    `I was paying it by road traffic instalments` IS `p3`
    `the stage reached` IS `p4`
    `days since the latest document was issued` IS `p5`
    `the time to pay the notice or my next instalment has run out` IS `p6`
    `the modified penalty still unpaid` IS `p7`
    `I have paid it all` IS `p8`
    `I have paid part of it` IS `p9`
    `I have elected to go to court` IS `p10`
    `the notice or the proceedings have been withdrawn` IS `p11`
    `the time limit for prosecuting has passed` IS `p12`
    `a time to pay order has been made` IS `p13`
    `my address ASGS class` IS `p14`
    `my postcode is shared with a regional or remote area` IS `p15`
    `my address is in the metropolitan region` IS `p16`
    `my postcode is shared with the metropolitan region` IS `p17`

§§ `For the person given an infringement notice (the baseline's seat, Part 3)`

-- Does Part 3 of the Act apply to my infringement notice?
-- k042: Jake, 20, an eRideable notice from WA Police under the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008.
#ASSERT `Does Part 3 of the Act apply to my infringement notice` `as the person given the notice` 20 `the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does Part 3 of the Act apply to my infringement notice` `as the person given the notice` 20 `the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008` TRUE EQUALS (`yes if` (`Does Part 3 apply to my infringement notice` (`a notice with` 20 `the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008` TRUE FALSE `the infringement notice` 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `Major Cities of Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE)))
-- s 12(3): under 17 at the time.
#ASSERT `Does Part 3 of the Act apply to my infringement notice` `as the person given the notice` 16 `the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008` TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does Part 3 of the Act apply to my infringement notice` `as the person given the notice` 16 `the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008` TRUE EQUALS (`yes if` (`Does Part 3 apply to my infringement notice` (`a notice with` 16 `the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008` TRUE FALSE `the infringement notice` 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `Major Cities of Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE)))
-- s 12(1).
#ASSERT `Does Part 3 of the Act apply to my infringement notice` `as the person given the notice` 20 `a law not listed in Schedule 1` TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does Part 3 of the Act apply to my infringement notice` `as the person given the notice` 20 `a law not listed in Schedule 1` TRUE EQUALS (`yes if` (`Does Part 3 apply to my infringement notice` (`a notice with` 20 `a law not listed in Schedule 1` TRUE FALSE `the infringement notice` 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `Major Cities of Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE)))
#ASSERT `Does Part 3 of the Act apply to my infringement notice` `as the person fined by a court` `an unasked number` `an unasked law` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

